From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OCTAGRAM-OS contributors <dev@octagram.invalid>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 20:00:00 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/1] std: recognize OCTAGRAM as an OS with a Unix PAL

This only permits build-std to attempt compiling std for OCTAGRAM.
The target's Unix PAL and libc ABI still need dedicated implementations
and conformance tests before std can be considered usable.

Upstream base: rust-lang/rust 342d74463af7dd3018ef6aa04dd5500c2deb5bd1

---
 library/std/build.rs | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/library/std/build.rs b/library/std/build.rs
index 98856b58d890..000000000000 100644
--- a/library/std/build.rs
+++ b/library/std/build.rs
@@ -54,6 +54,7 @@ fn main() {
         || target_os == "uefi"
         || target_os == "teeos"
         || target_os == "zkvm"
+        || target_os == "octagram"
         || target_os == "rtems"
         || target_os == "nuttx"
         || target_os == "cygwin"
